        "titulo": "The MASCULINE: it depends on the soul",
        "explicacao": "The MASCULINE: it depends on the soul. Now the masculine. Here the magic question comes in: does it have a soul? Masculine INANIMATE (no soul) → DOES NOT CHANGE. If the word is masculine and has no soul (an object, an idea, a place, a thing), it does not change in the accusative. It stays the same as the nominative. Notice: the word is identical. Дом is дом in the nominative and in the accusative. Example sentences follow. All inanimate objects stay the same: no mark, no change. Masculine ANIMATE (with a soul) → CHANGES (add one letter). If the word is masculine and has a soul (a person or an animal), it changes in the accusative. The change: add -А at the end (or -Я, if the word ends in -ь or -й). Rule: a masculine animate word ending in a consonant → +А. A masculine animate word ending in -ь → becomes -Я. A masculine animate word ending in -й → becomes -Я. Notice that you don't cut any letter. You add one at the end, -А or -Я. Example sentences follow. Notice that every word with a soul changed, and every one added a letter. The magic question in practice. Here is how to use the magic question to decide whether a masculine word changes. That is all. Ask. Answer. Apply. (Note that the animate masculine accusative is the same as the genitive: you will meet that in the next lessons.)",
