        "titulo": "The neuter, the master table and the accusative rule",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: The NEUTER: it never changes. The neuter is the easiest of all. It never changes in the accusative. It makes no difference whether it is an object, an idea or a thing. It stays the same as the nominative. Always. Notice that no neuter word changes. Ever. Example sentences follow. That is it. The neuter is neuter: no soul, no masculine/feminine endings to swap, no change. Full stop. STEP 2: The master table of the accusative. Here is the table that solves everything. STEP 3: The rule in three lines. If you forget everything else, memorise this: FEMININE: ALWAYS CHANGES (а→у, я→ю, ь does not change). MASCULINE: ASK \"HAS IT GOT A SOUL?\". If yes, add -а/-я. If not, no change. NEUTER: NEVER CHANGES. That is it. You have just mastered the accusative of nouns.",
